Monday Update
* Trade Alert: Sold Bit Digital calls for solid gain; buy AG and CAT calls*=
 Stocks advance as bargain-hunters swoop in for stocks bludgeoned last week=
Stocks are rising today as investors turn their attention back to tech and =
consumer stocks amid reports of outsized interest from retail investors in =
silver.Through midday, the Dow Jones Industrial average climbed by 218.02 p=
oints, or 0.7%, to 30,205.31, with S&amp;P 500 higher by 1.5% to 3,769.76 a=
nd Nasdaq up by 2.7% to 13,373.84. Consumer discretionary was the second-bi=
ggest gainer, with all sectors in the green after midday on Monday.Silver t=
raded 7.7% higher to $29 per troy ounce intraday, after touching as high as=
 $30 per troy ounce. Gold was up by 0.8% $1,862.3 per troy ounce. Oil advan=
ced by 1.7% to $53.06.The silver market is large and difficult to manipulat=
e and, unlike the equity market, there wasn't excessive short selling going=
 on with silver, Commerzbank said in a note to clients on Monday. Investors=
 were positioned "fairly optimistically" as per Jan. 26."The silver mania s=
parked by retail investors continues," Commerzbank analyst Eugen Weinberg s=
aid. "While the latest turmoil on the stock market was supposedly triggered=
 first and foremost by a so-called gamma squeeze -- additional stock-buying=
 forced by the purchase of call options -- we see little chances of any tig=
htening of the silver market via the terminal markets."A new proposal from =
a group of 10 GOP lawmakers calls for $1,000 checks per person, rather than=
 the $1,400 sum proposed by President Joe Biden, according to a report from=
 CNBC. That would bring the direct payments to $1,600, including the first =
payment authorized in December.In company news, IFF (IFF) launched a new br=
and identity to propel its transformation following the completion of its m=
erger with DuPont's Nutrition &amp; Biosciences business, also announced on=
 Monday. Shares were up by 14% intraday, the most on S&amp;P 500.Xerox (XRX=
) on Monday unveiled organizational changes to support plans to create thre=
e new businesses - software, financing and Innovation - that it were aimed =
aimed at delivering "long-term growth in 2021 and beyond." Shares jumped by=
 7.5%, the most on S&amp;P 500.While the precious metals were up, copper wa=
s down 0.4% to $3.54 per pound.Among energy ETFs, the United States Oil Fun=
d rose 1.7% to $35.65 and the United States Natural Gas Fund was up 11% to =
$10.46. Among precious-metal funds, the Market Vectors Gold Miners ETF was =
up 2.4% to $35.40 and SPDR Gold Shares were up 1.3% to $174.87. The iShares=
 Silver Trust was up 7.7% to $26.88.Portfolio: We sold BTBT calls for overa=
ll gain of 17.5% on Friday. Then we came into today flat. We have two new i=
deas for you. *CURRENT RECOMMENDATIONBit Digital Inc. (BTBT) February $17.5=
0 calls-- Symbol: BTBT210219C00017500-- Bought at $5.70 on Thursday, Jan. 2=
8. -- Sold half at $7.90 at the open Friday Jan 29 for a gain of 38.5%!-- S=
old second half Friday at $4.50 stop for 21% loss-- Overall gain was 17.5%-=
- This trade is complete *NEW RECOMMENDATIONSFirst Majestic Silver (AG) Feb=
ruary 17 calls-- Symbol: AG210219C00017000-- Order: Buy at $6.40 lmt day on=
ly-- If filled, set up to sell half at $8.30 lmt gtc and half at $11.20 lmt=
 gtc-- If filled, set stop at $4.40 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only*Cate=
rpillar (CAT) February 185 calls-- Symbol: CAT210219C00185000-- Order: Buy =
at $4.80 lmt day only-- If filled, set up to sell half at $6.25 lmt gtc and=
 half at $8.20 lmt gtc-- If filled, set stop at $3.35 stp, good after 10:30=
 a.m. ET only*Thanks for reading,Jon D. MarkmanAll recommendations are for =
monthly options expiring on the third Friday of the specified month unless =
